# WHITELIST layout.
#
# This repo lives inside ~/.claude, which Claude Code fills with runtime
# clutter (sessions, caches, daemon state, logs, etc.). Rather than chase
# every new noise file with a blacklist entry, we ignore EVERYTHING at the
# repo root by default and then explicitly re-include only the paths we
# actually track.
#
# To track a new top-level path, add a line:  !/<name>
# (this works for both files and directories).

# Ignore all top-level entries by default.
/*

# Re-include tracked top-level entries.
!/.gitignore
!/channel
!/CLAUDE.md
!/docs
!/README.md
!/RTK.md
!/scripts
!/settings.json
!/setup.sh
!/skills
!/tests

# Noise that can appear INSIDE re-included dirs, ignored everywhere.
**/__pycache__/
**/node_modules/
*.pyc
*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
quality-results/

# Feature worktrees live at <repo-root>/.claude/worktrees/<name>. In this repo the
# root IS ~/.claude, so they land at ~/.claude/.claude/worktrees/ — already covered
# by the /* rule above, but spelled out so the intent survives a layout change.
**/.claude/worktrees/
